cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use rust-store in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "rust-store: multi-backend data engine core (GQL planning, permissions, SQL dialect translation)"
abstract: >-
  A pure-logic Rust core with no IO, clock or randomness: it parses the MongoDB-style GQL tree
  dialect, applies role and field-level permission checks, injects owner conditions, resolves
  computed columns, plans one native command per backend and translates that command to
  parameterized MongoDB, MySQL, SQLite and PostgreSQL. Exposed to Node.js through the napi-rs
  binding rust-store-node and to Python through the PyO3 binding rust-store-py; the hosts
  nodejs-store and py-store own driver IO.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "leo"
    email: "coen_ddt@qq.com"
